# session/identity -- URL-normalization rules for Chrome window identity.
#
# session-mgr keys each Chrome window's placement on its ACTIVE-TAB URL (read
# from Chrome's SNSS session file), not its title -- the title carries volatile
# noise (unread counts like "Inbox (7)", the active tab, live page updates) that
# broke restore. A URL is normalized to "host/path" with the query and fragment
# dropped, which already kills most of that churn.
#
# This file collapses URLs whose PATH is also volatile down to a stable id. Each
# rule is one line:
#
#     <url-regex> :: <canonical-id>
#
# The left side is a Python regex matched (re.search, UNANCHORED) against the
# normalized "host/path"; the right side is the LITERAL id every matching window
# collapses to (not a regex). First matching rule wins. A line starting with #
# is a comment; blanks are ignored. Edits apply live (the watcher reloads on
# save). Show the loaded rules + how live Chrome windows resolve with
# `session-mgr identity`.
#
# Gmail rewrites its path with message ids as you read mail, so pin it to one id
# so the window keeps its place regardless of which thread is open.
^mail\.google\.com :: mail.google.com
